            "parent_column": "right",
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Add On: Kryon Grand Canyon Day Tour",
            "text": "<p>Led by Lee Carroll & Monika Muranyi on June 9, 2025 (Monday)</p><p>6:00 AM – 8:00 PM</p>",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>Includes: Kryon Channeling, Deluxe Coaches, Professional Tour Guides, Lunch & Snack Box, Water Bottle, Tips to guides & bus drivers.<br/><br/>Pick-up & Drop-off location:<a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir//Location%3A+995+Upper+Red+Rock+Loop+Rd%2C+Sedona%2C+AZ+86336/@34.8573133%2C-111.828259%2C14z/data%3D%214m8%214m7%211m0%211m5%211m1%211s0x872da731a37089a9%3A0xecc50249f7694a05%212m2%211d-111.8306923%212d34.8481845?entry=ttu\">Sedona Performing Arts Center</a>, 995 Upper Red Rock Loop Rd, Sedona, AZ 86336<br/><br/>Important Note: Buses will be departing at 6:00 AM. Please make sure to arrive at least 30 mins<em>before</em>, to allow time for your parking, check-in and boarding. We can not wait for late arrivals on this tour. Make sure to be on time so you don’t miss the tour!</p>",
            "dropdown_html": "<ul>\n<li>Use this text to answer questions in as much detail as possible for your customers.</li>\n<li>Use this text to answer questions in as much detail as possible for your customers.</li>\n</ul>",
            "dropdown_image": "shopify://shop_images/656.jpg",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "643bace9-4996-4be4-b931-2de728a157a3": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "parent_column": "right",
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Caral Pyramid",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>Caral is thought to be one of the oldest known cities in the Western Hemisphere. The Caral civilization was pre-Columbian. It remains a mystery as to why the city was abandoned.</p><p>One of the largest Pyramids in the complex is known as the Pirámide Mayor and is almost 100 feet tall and is considered to be as old as the Egyptian pyramids. </p>",
            "dropdown_html": "<ul>\n<li>Use this text to answer questions in as much detail as possible for your customers.</li>\n<li>Use this text to answer questions in as much detail as possible for your customers.</li>\n</ul>",
            "dropdown_image": "shopify://shop_images/Peru-Tour-Caral-Enhanced.jpg",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#f4f5f7"
          }
        },
        "cab40b70-71f5-4157-900c-344ccf2d5e06": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "parent_column": "right",
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Amaru Muru",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>Amaru Muru also known as “Hayu Marca or Willka Uta: “Place of the sun or gate of the gods.” This magnanimous rock structure is surrounded by mystery and ancient legends. A stunning doorway is carved into the ancient rock wall and faces east, toward Lake Titicaca, the Island of the Sun in Bolivia and the distant, sacred snow-capped mountains.</p>",
            "dropdown_html": "<ul>\n<li>Use this text to answer questions in as much detail as possible for your customers.</li>\n<li>Use this text to answer questions in as much detail as possible for your customers.</li>\n</ul>",
            "dropdown_image": "shopify://shop_images/Peru-Tour-Amaru-Muru.jpg",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#f4f5f7"
          }
        },
        "bd48c292-e8fb-405b-9fc2-3e92ec363226": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "parent_column": "right",
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Island of the Sun Bolivia",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>We will take a private boat to visit the beautiful<strong> Isla Del Sol. O</strong>riginally known as Titi Khar'ka, the 'rock of the puma' from which Lake Titicaca gets its name. <strong>A sacred place for the Aymara people </strong>and believed to be <strong>the birthplace of the Inca Empire</strong>. There are over 80 ancient ruins that predate the Inca empire to include the Chinkana and Pillkukayna,</p>",
            "dropdown_html": "<ul>\n<li>Use this text to answer questions in as much detail as possible for your customers.</li>\n<li>Use this text to answer questions in as much detail as possible for your customers.</li>\n</ul>",
            "dropdown_image": "shopify://shop_images/Peru-Tour-Stone-Table.jpg",
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#f4f5f7"
          }
        }
